[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160712"] :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x+y+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,u-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=u-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+(u-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "405ab8f8-79dd-58fa-bf1e-c63cc69f4824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127/selection/0786bc1a26ed24b6f61a4e903dc9d5d976f625dc623e01dbcd98d98839ae6296" :answer/id #uuid "6dc79d0a-8c51-580f-a70e-03efc7799663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" :answer/id #uuid "26aa5890-8eea-56e1-bb15-1ae9d870ebb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "7c1d2d62-ef56-51e9-a12e-36f44901e7e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "f0c444b7-89a7-5cc0-84ed-a2a363a5d2da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2aca348c-b9d8-59de-9e27-7a16826b1f7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161127/selection/0786bc1a26ed24b6f61a4e903dc9d5d976f625dc623e01dbcd98d98839ae6296" :answer-field/choices ["q-161127/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-161127/selection/0786bc1a26ed24b6f61a4e903dc9d5d976f625dc623e01dbcd98d98839ae6296" "q-161127/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" "q-161127/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-161127/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161127" :question/id #uuid "18dc2b17-918c-58cb-b73a-247a9dacca45" :question/math-academy-id "q-161127" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-2yz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,u,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+-{1}^{2}+-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & ={x}^{2}-2yz\\,{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(u+v)^{2}-2uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-2yz\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+u{v}^{2}]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}+2{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{2}{3}v+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161127/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161127"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132/selection/a01d27cce5425905ea9a009d762a7cd19508990f68fbe9029c3d3eedfc846e35" :answer/id #uuid "ee3f3752-41e8-57cf-b880-71e4d4df98c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({v}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132/selection/6d6cee1dc3694e99fe8466ef002646dd5a28b599d4edd42cc459187d86536c77" :answer/id #uuid "e8da5aa1-8d0e-55ed-91ee-d844c9cdf4b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{3}+{v}^{3})\\sqrt{16{v}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132/selection/95b98cbe1a186ec2d30ee2b75fbe327b8cdafbea16993906a4345d1cf2afbcdc" :answer/id #uuid "a2b16629-a7fe-5f86-b675-3f8d563a25dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({v}^{2}+2u)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132/selection/f82d253c7e9a90ce436b8b0016bf8602d4c16c97ffed7781020fb81e945c3f39" :answer/id #uuid "11f6382a-1260-56a0-853e-48b8938ccdb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132/selection/ab7aec10c2d9be6f49e86de5036b5af9fed551e15cb7976caf8700eda1bfef39" :answer/id #uuid "e2caf314-d7f1-59d5-9aa2-0020f0effcdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u+v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da9cec8d-74e8-52c2-ae1f-8e2db9fb815a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161132/selection/f82d253c7e9a90ce436b8b0016bf8602d4c16c97ffed7781020fb81e945c3f39" :answer-field/choices ["q-161132/selection/a01d27cce5425905ea9a009d762a7cd19508990f68fbe9029c3d3eedfc846e35" "q-161132/selection/6d6cee1dc3694e99fe8466ef002646dd5a28b599d4edd42cc459187d86536c77" "q-161132/selection/95b98cbe1a186ec2d30ee2b75fbe327b8cdafbea16993906a4345d1cf2afbcdc" "q-161132/selection/f82d253c7e9a90ce436b8b0016bf8602d4c16c97ffed7781020fb81e945c3f39" "q-161132/selection/ab7aec10c2d9be6f49e86de5036b5af9fed551e15cb7976caf8700eda1bfef39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161132" :question/id #uuid "9de41d79-7798-5e1d-b077-c1d9dece4dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161132" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xy+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xy+z)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =u.{u}^{2}+2v \\\\  & ={u}^{3}+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242/selection/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837" :answer/id #uuid "4e40515d-5766-55e4-b6e4-553a2fe93566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242/selection/51b7e71ac415d62fcd6302db1c518c0badce55dda03eceebe662e87a5996a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "e71a2a0e-7d8e-5f9c-96c9-d38be230e6c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer/id #uuid "8dedb06b-f2f4-55fe-8704-ab360bc75b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" :answer/id #uuid "67eefd6c-c0ea-524a-9ba7-5c7cbf0c83bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "be5748ed-9ce7-5c05-85e1-5a02dce47e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f5a4b86-941d-5ccc-bc6e-ab729cae9ce1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161242/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-161242/selection/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837" "q-161242/selection/51b7e71ac415d62fcd6302db1c518c0badce55dda03eceebe662e87a5996a8b4" "q-161242/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" "q-161242/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" "q-161242/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161242" :question/id #uuid "28d5c29f-26b0-57e9-aad1-66eedd869c86" :question/math-academy-id "q-161242" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}x(y+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2u,\\,y=-3v,\\,z=4v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u,\\,-3v,\\,4v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-3v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-3v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-3,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-8,\\,-6⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-8,\\,-6⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =x(y+z)\\,{|}_{x=2u\\,y=-3v\\,z=4v} \\\\  & =2u(-3v+4v) \\\\  & =2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}x(y+z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2uv\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =5\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161242/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161242"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285/selection/b39cefdfa6409028660d8a8cf38d73fcc8d7adc9d5747c66a6990c5ac266025f" :answer/id #uuid "596dbeb3-408d-5fb6-a655-817dd5cef98e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u)\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285/selection/b3826b0e14b423d811f67d144e9819419b6e4ae63b9af03ae6702696d7d0f7c5" :answer/id #uuid "a7964e9d-76b7-5ad5-b382-68d931c46aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(uv-u)\\sqrt{2u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285/selection/9bc40a1da31c60f1bc1db425b4d537217a25d0fedcc91ea2511e8c709c81f86f" :answer/id #uuid "eb74fdae-5d71-513e-809f-0ce1d8837e0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{2}v\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285/selection/fc44331bb8f0268e5ea65d06ab4ac4652a656d0c3765db3a8f6bdf432cda5421" :answer/id #uuid "d0485668-af8d-5054-afce-098e624da5f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}{v}^{2}+2)\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285/selection/9718e2147e7785e564222517633b543c947280403d0f94a87e592cc30b77e4b9" :answer/id #uuid "0a5d7a1a-f9da-5b04-8575-04d08b2941b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u{v}^{2}+u)\\sqrt{2u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca6f00c2-c2bb-56f2-82ab-caa97e392a0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161285/selection/b39cefdfa6409028660d8a8cf38d73fcc8d7adc9d5747c66a6990c5ac266025f" :answer-field/choices ["q-161285/selection/b39cefdfa6409028660d8a8cf38d73fcc8d7adc9d5747c66a6990c5ac266025f" "q-161285/selection/b3826b0e14b423d811f67d144e9819419b6e4ae63b9af03ae6702696d7d0f7c5" "q-161285/selection/9bc40a1da31c60f1bc1db425b4d537217a25d0fedcc91ea2511e8c709c81f86f" "q-161285/selection/fc44331bb8f0268e5ea65d06ab4ac4652a656d0c3765db3a8f6bdf432cda5421" "q-161285/selection/9718e2147e7785e564222517633b543c947280403d0f94a87e592cc30b77e4b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161285" :question/id #uuid "9607f95f-91e9-5d9d-a4a0-4b48dd08d587" :question/math-academy-id "q-161285" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}+y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨-u,\\,-u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}{z}^{2}+y)\\,{|}_{x=-u\\,y=-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =(-u)^{2}\\cdot (-v)^{2}-u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u)\\sqrt{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161285/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161285"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
